011,"counterion":"[Cl-].[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-005017","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol/water partition coefficient of compound 3 was determined using a shake-flask method. PBS buffered bi-distillated water (100 mL, phosphate buffer, c(PO4 3-) = 10 mM, c(NaCl) = 0.15 M, pH adjusted to 7.4 with HCl) and n-octanol (100 mL) were shaken together using a laboratory shaker for 72 h to allow saturation of both phases. 1 mg of 3 was mixed in 1 mL of aqueous and organic phase, respectively for 10 min using a laboratory vortexer. The resultant emulsion was centrifuged (3000 x g, 5 min) to separate the phases. The concentrations of 3 in the organic and aqueous phases were then determined using UV absorbance spectroscopy (230 nm). Log DpH was defined as the logarithm of the ratio of the concentrations of the complex in the organic and aqueous phases; the value reported is the mean of three separate determinations."}],"ccdc":["AQIRAU"]}